;*******************************************************;;	'SCSIM.History';;	Written by:;	;					Gus Andrade;;	Modified for new card by:;;					Matt Gulick.;					Started June 1,1989;;	Copyright Apple Computer, Inc. 1988,89;	All rights reserved.;;*******************************************************					STRING		PASCAL					BLANKS		OFF					PAGESIZE	70					PRINT		NOGEN					PRINT		NOMDIR					MACHINE		M65816;					IMPORT		;					ENTRY							PRINT		OFF;					INCLUDE		'SCSIM.Equates';					INCLUDE		'Common.Equ.Src';					INCLUDE		'HW.Equ.Src';					INCLUDE		'M16.MEMORY';					INCLUDE		'M16.UTIL';					INCLUDE		'M16.MISCTOOL'					PRINT		ON					EJECT;*******************************************************;;	'SCSIM.History';;	This file contains the rev history for the SCSI;	Manager.  All major Modifications, Design Changes;	and Bug Fixes are described in the following text.;;	Copyright Apple Computer, Inc. 1988-1989;	All rights reserved.;;*******************************************************;;	REVISION HISTORY:;;	System Bug Fix Manager	Creator	Description of bug fixed;;	Date:		Version:		;;	5-26-88		D0.01	GAA	Start SCSI Manager code development;;	12-1-88		0.01A	GAA	Alpha release of manager;;	12-12-88	0.02A	GAA;						1.	Bug fix for crash on startup with;							no cards present;						2.	Added Autosensing support code;						3.	Bus float check looks for bus free;					   		to tell if card present.;;	12-30-88	0.03A	GAA;						1.	Fixed a crash bug when autosense was;							enabled and mode sense call failed.;						2.	Fixed a bug where pdmaoff was droping;							a byte between data chaining;							instructions;						3.	Added code to zero out some of the;							internal parameters in the old SCSI;							card to force to rebuild its SDATS;							when launching a Prodos 8 application;;	01-07-89	0.04	GAA;						1.	Fixed a bug where the memory I;							allocated for myself was disposed of;							when an error was encountered during;							startup but the code segment was not;							because I returned to the Supervisory;							Dispatcher with carry cleared.  This;							made the system crash in various ways.;;	01-15-89	0.05	GAA;						1.	Added code to increment the BUSY flag;							on ENTRY to the SCSI Manager and;							decrement on exit to prevent access to;							desk accessories during calls to the;							SCSI Manager. Long delays in Desk Accs;							can  lockup targets and the Manager.;						2.	Phase Handler will no longer hang on a;							call which has timed out.;						3.	Modified the Logical unit scanner to;							stop the scan for LUs on a scsi ID if;							access to an LU fails. Will not;							install the LU that failed and ones;							that follow.;						4.	Now issuing a Test Unit Ready prior to;							Inquiry call to force target to clear;							sense data generated by the the bus;							reset to the bus during the scsi card;							slot scan.;;	01-23-89	0.06	GAA;						1.	Fixed infinite loop bug when there was;							no jumper installed on the initiator;							priority jumper on the OLD scsi card.;;	01-24-89	0.07	GAA;						1.	Fixed a bug where the Manager was;							dropping devices because the 5380 was;							sending $00 instead of $80 during the;							message out phase for the identify.;							This appears to go out because the;							target select register was set to the;							initiator priority after we have won;							arbitration and are trying select the;							target.  Also the assert data bus bit;							is set every time I come into phase;							handler to make sure that the bus is;							turned on.;;	01-27-89	0.08	GAA;						1.	Fixed a bug where the phase bits were;							being set before set before checking to;							see if request was asserted.;;	01-30-89	0.09	GAA;						1.	Bug fix: returned $FE00 for a call which;							failed with a check condition ($02).;							Should have returned $FE02.  This;							occurred only when a call failed and no;							autosense pointer was provided.;;	02-08-89	0.0A	GAA;						1.	Fixed a bug where the last byte of each;							DCMOVE data chain instruction was being;							dropped when multiple data chaining;							instructions were issued to the SCSI;							Manager with one call.;						2.	Fixed a bug where the data chaining prog.;							counter was not being bumped to the next;							instruction for DCMOVE instructions.;						3.	Fixed a bug where the savepointers;							routine was not setting the pointer;							for the save field properly.;						4.	Added code to add the contents of the;							DCoffset field to the address field;							in the DCMOVE instruction each time a;							DCMOVE instruction is accessed.;						5.	Moved the Select timeout back to 250;							millisecs from from 350 millisecs.;;	02-15-89	0.0B	GAA;						1.	Fixed a bug where the transfer count;							update routine was not updating the;							high word of the transfer count.;						2.	Bug fix where the transfer count;							field was not updated when data was;							being written to a target.;						3.	Bug fix: When two SCSI cards installed;							with different initiator priorities;							the entries in the I/O table for logical;							unit encoding were shifted by one;							logical unit.;;	03-06-89	0.0C	GAA;						1.	Bug fix: was returning $FE00 when;							autosensing was enabled for a call;							and the autosense call succeeded on;							a device specific $801B.;						2.	Added the code to the SCSI Manager for;							WarmStart and shutdown.;						3.	Removed the check for REQ in the;							Osend_bytes routine It was to there to;							try and prevent the problem with the;							transfer count being off by one on;							writes to a target.  The fix did not;							work!!!  Drivers must insure that the;							number of bytes specified in the;							req/xfer count field of the parameter;							block  match the number of bytes;							specified in the CDB.;;	03-17-89			1.	NO CHANGES;;	03-21-89	0.0D	GAA;						1.	The initial release for beta.;						2.	Changed the ID assignment to match;							the format of the ID fields as;							defined by the device dispatcher.;							The ID field now is a 32 bit ENTRY;							with the low word set to the slot;							number and the next word an ID;							incrementing from $0001 to $FFFF.;						3.	Added the detection for the rev C;							SCSI rom.  If the rom installed is;							not a rev. C a message will be;							displayed on the screen and that;							card will be installed in the device;							list (for the time being).;;	03-17-89			1.	NO CHANGES;;	04-03-89	0.0E	GAA;						1.	Fixed a bug where the SDRSTOCHECK;							counter was not being reloaded when;							booting from a floppy when the call;							to ASSIGNID subroutine call was made.;;						2.	Fixed a bug where index to the sdr;							was pointing to the slot field instead;							of the link field for the next SDR in;							the list.  This caused the SDR to;							contain erroneous ID information during;							the ID assignment PROCess.;;						3.	Fixed a bug in the zap_oldcard routine;							to mask off the external slot bit prior;							using it to turn on the $CNXX space for;							a card.;;	04-07-89	0.0F	GAA;						1.	Added a vector to store the address of;							my zero page so the Snooper CDA can;							have access to my handles and access;							to my tables for display purposes.;;						2.	Fixed a bug in the Find_sdr routine.;							The last accessed pointers were not;							being updated and this in turn was;							forcing the scan through the entire;							SDR table to find the requested device.;;						3.	Bug fix in irq handler where was;							returning the wrong polarity on the;							carry when an interrupt was serviced;							for a SCSI card.;;						4.	Bug fix in irq handler where the;							pointer to the record in the I/O;							table was not pointing to the slot;							field in the record when trying to;							check to see if a slot had a scsi;							card installed with a possible;							interrupt which needed servicing.;;						5.	Fixed bug with auto sensing where;							the slot number portion of the ID was;							not being set prior to issuing a;							Request sense call for autosense.;;	05-15-89	0.10	MSG;						1.	Started to restructure the SCSI;							Manager Source code from one file;							into smaller funtional modules.;							This will hopefully aid int the;							modification of the manager to be;							more flexable in either;							communicating with non-Apple SCSI;							Cards and also adding the Sandwich;							card when it is available.;;	6-10-89		0.11	MSG;						1.	Fixed bug in claim devices call.;;	7-10-89		1.01	MSG;						1.	Merged Latest SCSI Manager from the;							Finale GS/OS 5.0 Disk with the files;							under development for the new card and;							GS/OS 5.1;;	7-18-89		2.01	MSG;						1.	Fixed Minor errors due to translation;						2.	Updated the Routine Headers;						3.	Trimed down code size, removed 'MOVE;							BYTES' and modified the 'CLEAR MEMORY';							Routines.  The OS Move Info call is now;							used, and the clear memory is done by;							by the Move Info Call.;;	7-24-89		2.02	MSG;						1.	Fixed error from translation (making;							this version a working pre-cacoon;							version), cleaned up the code and;							comments.  Also updated the entry and;							exit information for each routine.;;	7-24-89 through;	8-24-89		2.03	MSG;						1.	Fixed problem in Cocoon Read and Write;							where I was hitting the 53c80 every time;							I restarted after an interupt stopped DMA.;							This was causing data to be lost.;						2.	Took all the JSR to bit wiggle routines;							and placed the code inline replacing the;							JSRs.  This improved the polled I/O from;							200+ milliseconds to 72+ per byte sent.;						3.	No longer allowing interupts to stop DMA.;							On large transfers DMA was getting;							interrupted, for some unknown reason,;							approx every $200 bytes of data.  This;							slowed down the overall performance by a;							significant amount.  IRQ's are still safe;							however since an IRQ window is opened every;							time a bank boundry is crossed.  This would;							normally be every 65.5 milliseconds at 64k;							data with a 1meg/sec transfer rate.;;	8-29-89		2.04	MSG;						1.	At the time of shutdown, the Manager was;							doing an unbind_irq OS Call.  This call was;							failing do to the OS being busy.  Added cade;							to place a vector at $e1103A.  The 4 bytes;							at that location were imported, and a JML;							was put in it's place.  This is called just;							before the start app. is called.  The code;							jumped to installs a Notify Proc to inform;							the manager when a shutdown or os switch is;							taking place. This then calls unbind_irq.;							It's messy, but it works.;;	9-13-89		2.05	MSG;						1.	Fixed a problem in the manager and DMA.  If;							the IRQs were disabled on entry to the Manager,;							DMA would hang when DMA was told to allow irqs.;							The manager now tells sandwich to ignor irqs;							if the I processor status bit was set on entry;							to the manager.;;	10-3-89		2.06	MSG;						1.	Added Pseudo DMA Mode for cocoon.;						2.	Cleaned up the manager.  Fixed a bug where the;							return count had a $FFFF in the high word.;							Added a few minor speed improvments.;;	10-10-89	2.07	MSG;						1.	Combined Common routines.;						2.	Fixed Pseudo DMA.  It now actually works.;						3.	Fixed some bugs in the messaging system.;;	10-27-89	2.08	MSG;						1.	Fixed p8 launch bug where system would hang;							forever.;						2.	Fixed bug that cause infinite beeping loop on;							shutdown and restart.;						3.	Remainder of bugs seem to be due to un reliable;							data through the unterminated cocoon card.;;	01-25-91	6.00	MSG;						1.	Added ROM Writes to each Phase handler for Timing;							and performance evaluations.;						2.	Modified code to always do DMA to System Ram;							regardless of the DMA Switch.  Most Directories;							are read into Bank 0 and would benifit from DMA;							even if the Expansion RAM could not support DMA.;;*******************************************************;history				PROC					ENDP					EJECT					END					